UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 715-30-35-7, interest cost is computed as the beginning projected benefit obligation (PBO) multiplied by the discount rate. This reflects the increase in the PBO due to the passage of time, moving one year closer to benefit payment. The discount rate reflects rates at which pension obligations could be effectively settled.
Wrong (B): Fair value of plan assets multiplied by the expected return rate computes the expected return on plan assets, a separate pension cost component that reduces net periodic pension cost.
Wrong (C): Service cost is an independent component representing new benefits earned in the current period. It is not multiplied by the discount rate to derive interest cost.
