-- Q3294: Pension and Postretirement Benefits [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 715-30-35-9, the expected return on plan assets reduces net periodic pension cost because investment earnings on plan assets help offset the pension obligation. The expected (not actual) return is used for income statement purposes to smooth earnings volatility.
Wrong (A): The expected return does not increase pension cost. It operates as an offset, reducing the total net periodic pension cost reported in earnings.
Wrong (B): The expected return is a component of net periodic pension cost in earnings. The difference between actual and expected returns is recognized in OCI under ASC 715-30-35-25, but the expected return itself flows through earnings.
Wrong (D): The expected return directly affects pension cost as one of its defined components. It is not ignored in the calculation.$EXPL$
