  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 715-30-35, ending plan assets equal beginning assets plus actual return plus contributions minus benefits paid. Solving: $4,500,000 = $4,000,000 + Return + $350,000 - $400,000, so Return = $550,000. The actual return captures all investment gains and losses during the period.
Wrong (B): $500,000 is the simple difference between ending and beginning asset values ($4,500,000 - $4,000,000), but this ignores the net effect of contributions received and benefits paid during the year.
Wrong (C): $150,000 results from subtracting contributions from the net asset change ($500,000 - $350,000), incorrectly treating benefits paid as zero.
