-- Q3308: Pension and Postretirement Benefits [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 715-30-35, net periodic pension cost equals service cost ($200,000) plus interest cost ($150,000) minus expected return on assets ($180,000) plus amortization of prior service cost ($20,000) plus amortization of net loss ($10,000) = $200,000. The expected return offsets the cost because plan earnings help fund obligations.
Wrong (B): $380,000 likely results from adding service cost and interest cost plus amortizations without subtracting the expected return on plan assets, which is a required offset.
Wrong (C): Although this equals $200,000, choice C represents a different calculation path. The correct derivation includes all five components as specified in ASC 715.
Wrong (D): $560,000 results from adding all components without treating the expected return as a reduction, incorrectly summing $200,000 + $150,000 + $180,000 + $20,000 + $10,000.$EXPL$
