-- Q3315: Fund-to-Government-Wide Reconciliation [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under GASB Statement No. 33 and the modified accrual basis per GASB Statement No. 34, revenue must be both measurable and available (collected within the availability period, typically 60 days after year-end). Since the $300,000 is expected to be collected 90 days after year-end, it fails the availability criterion and is reported as deferred inflows of resources.
Wrong (A): Revenue recognition requires meeting both measurable and available criteria under modified accrual. Collection beyond 60 days means the taxes are not available for current-period recognition.
Wrong (C): The taxes were levied and are measurable, so they must be recorded. They appear on the balance sheet as deferred inflows rather than being omitted entirely.
Wrong (D): Deferred inflows of resources are distinct from liabilities. The government does not owe the amount to anyone; rather, it has not yet met the availability criterion for revenue recognition.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3315;

-- Q3318: Fund-to-Government-Wide Reconciliation [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under GASB Statement No. 34, paragraph 77, capital outlay ($2,000,000) is added back in the reconciliation because it is an expenditure in governmental funds but a capitalized asset government-wide, while depreciation ($500,000) is subtracted because it is an expense government-wide but not recognized in funds. The net adjustment is +$2,000,000 - $500,000 = +$1,500,000.
Wrong (A): Adding only $2,000,000 accounts for the capital outlay reclassification but ignores the $500,000 depreciation expense that must be subtracted on the government-wide statements.
Wrong (B): $2,500,000 incorrectly adds both the capital outlay and depreciation, but depreciation reduces net position on government-wide statements and must be subtracted.
Wrong (C): Subtracting $500,000 accounts only for depreciation and ignores the $2,000,000 capital outlay that must be added back when converting from modified to full accrual.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3318;

-- Q3321: Fund-to-Government-Wide Reconciliation [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under GASB Statement No. 34, paragraph 80, governmental funds use modified accrual, where interest on long-term debt is recognized only when legally due and payable. Accrued but unmatured interest does not appear as a fund liability. On government-wide statements using full accrual, the $75,000 must be accrued and reported as a liability on the statement of net position.
Wrong (A): Under modified accrual, the debt service fund only recognizes interest when it is due and payable. Accrued but unmatured interest is not reported as a current liability in any governmental fund.
Wrong (C): Accrued interest is not merely a note disclosure item. Government-wide statements require recognition on the face of the statement of net position under full accrual accounting.
Wrong (D): Accrued interest payable is a liability, not a deferred outflow of resources. Deferred outflows relate to items such as pension and OPEB adjustments under GASB standards.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3321;

-- Q3322: Fund-to-Government-Wide Reconciliation [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under GASB Statement No. 34, paragraphs 77-79, net position equals fund balance plus capital assets minus long-term liabilities plus deferred outflows minus deferred inflows: $3,500,000 + $15,000,000 - $9,000,000 + $400,000 - $200,000 = $9,700,000. The reconciliation must account for all items differing between modified accrual and full accrual.
Wrong (B): $9,500,000 likely omits the deferred outflows ($400,000) or deferred inflows ($200,000), producing an incomplete reconciliation that ignores pension-related adjustments.
Wrong (C): $10,100,000 may result from adding deferred outflows and inflows instead of netting them, or from misapplying the direction of one adjustment in the reconciliation.
Wrong (D): $8,900,000 may result from double-counting one of the deferred amounts or misapplying the sign on capital assets or long-term liabilities in the reconciliation.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3322;

-- Q3325: Fund-to-Government-Wide Reconciliation [hard/L2]
