  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under GASB Statement No. 34, paragraphs 77-79, reconciliations between governmental fund statements and government-wide statements must be presented either on the face of the fund financial statements or in an accompanying schedule. This ensures transparency about the differences between the two reporting perspectives.
Wrong (A): Notes disclosure alone is insufficient. GASB requires the reconciliation to appear on the face of the statements or in an accompanying schedule, giving it greater prominence than note disclosure.
Wrong (B): The MD&A provides narrative analysis but is not the required location for the reconciliation. The reconciliation must appear in the basic financial statements section.
