-- Q3351: Prospective Analysis and Forecasting [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under CVP analysis principles consistent with ASC 420-10, the contribution margin ratio equals ($24 - $12) / $24 = 50%. Breakeven in sales dollars equals fixed costs divided by the CM ratio: $360,000 / 0.50 = $720,000, equivalent to 30,000 units at $24 per unit.
Wrong (B): $360,000 equals total fixed costs, which would be breakeven only if the CM ratio were 100% (i.e., zero variable costs). With $12 variable cost per unit, the CM ratio is 50%.
Wrong (C): $180,000 is half the fixed costs and does not correspond to any valid breakeven formula. It may result from incorrectly applying the CM ratio in the numerator instead of the denominator.
Wrong (D): $540,000 does not result from the correct breakeven formula. It may reflect an arithmetic error such as using a 67% CM ratio instead of the correct 50%.$EXPL$
